Package: zutable
Title: Typed Tables Queried with SQL Clauses
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: A data frame that always knows its schema: the name, logical
    type and nullability of every column, with the types of 'Apache Arrow'.
    Queries are written in the bracket, with the clauses of SQL (structured
    query language) as named arguments over bare column names, and are
    translated into typed expressions over a closed vocabulary, so the
    schema of every result, and every type error, is known before any data
    is read. Existing columns are updated in place, a table can be frozen
    against further change, and grouping, sorting, joining and reducing run
    on a cache-conscious kernel whose header other packages can use through
    'LinkingTo'.
